# ============================================================================
# TAU-NOMIC TUTORIAL 08 - THE EDGES
# What stays genuinely outside the decidable core - and why naming it
# precisely is design, not defeat
# ============================================================================
#
# Series so far: specs are decidable values (1), deciding replaces voting
# (2), the constitution lives as a run (3), it judges actions (4), the
# ratchet makes permanence provable (5), a real eternity clause runs (6),
# and the honest map shows what reduces and which form scales (7).
#
# Final question: WHAT IS LEFT? Every closed formal core has edges it
# cannot contain. The design principle of tau-nomic is not to deny them -
# it is: MAKE EVERY EDGE SMALL, EXPLICIT, AND GOVERNED BY THE SAME NOMIC.
# What remains after that is always one of two kinds:
#   (A) a hard fact about the physical world (no system closes it), or
#   (B) a political question about power and values (no formalism should).
#
# Run me:  tau -q < nomic_08_the_edges.tau
# Verified against: Tau 0.7.0-alpha, build 240788e (alpha syntax may drift).
# ============================================================================

# EXPECTED-RESULTS: F T F

set charvar off

# ============================================================================
# EDGE 1: TRANSLATION - who says what the words mean?
# ============================================================================
# Part 6 encoded Art. 14(3) ("expropriation only with compensation") as
# o38 -> o39. But someone could encode it as o38 -> o31 ("...only by
# statute"). Both LOOK plausible. Are they the same law?

normalize (({ o38[t]=1 -> o39[t]=1 }) = ({ o38[t]=1 -> o31[t]=1 })).
# => F
#    Tau PROVES the two readings differ - no two people can silently
#    believe they agreed while holding different laws. But notice what
#    Tau cannot do: it cannot say WHICH reading is faithful to the
#    German text. That act - translation of meaning into structure -
#    carries real power (whoever frames the encoding frames the law),
#    and it stays human. Edge type (B).
#
# What Tau DOES eliminate: fights over mere reformulation. The correct
# contrapositive of the core is provably THE SAME law:

normalize (({ o1[t]=1 -> o4[t]=1 }) = ({ o4[t]!=1 -> o1[t]!=1 })).
# => T
#    Different words, same value. Debate collapses to substance.
#
# And a subtlety your two-valued intuition will get wrong: replacing
# "not equal to 1" by "equal to 0" is NOT the same statement here -

normalize (({ o1[t]=1 -> o4[t]=1 }) = ({ o4[t]=0 -> o1[t]=0 })).
# => F
#    - because the tau algebra is ATOMLESS: a stream's value is a SPEC,
#    and between 0 and 1 lie infinitely many values. "o4 != 1" admits
#    them; "o4 = 0" excludes all of them. Even the translator's logic
#    is held to a finer standard than two-valued intuition.

# ============================================================================
# EDGE 2: ENFORCEMENT - a theorem does not switch off a server
# ============================================================================
# Parts 3-6 proved verdicts: code 8, forbidden, on every path. But the
# verdict is a VALUE. Whether the datacenter API call is actually blocked
# is a fact about actuators, not algebras - EVERY governance system,
# legal or digital, ends at this same edge. Type (A).
#
# What tau-nomic does at this edge: shrinks it to a minimal, auditable,
# judgment-free gate ("execute only if the verdict allows") - a component
# with no interpretive latitude of its own, hence nothing in it to
# persuade or corrupt - and keeps everything with CONTENT (what is legal, what
# is permanent, what follows) inside the decidable core. Compare: an
# LLM guardrail is a PERSUADABLE judge at the same position; here the
# gate has nothing to be persuaded about. And inside the run itself,
# there is no bypass: the machine of parts 3-6 has no admin input, no
# override stream - unbypassability is architectural, not promised.

# ============================================================================
# EDGE 3: IDENTITY - the algebra cannot know who is speaking
# ============================================================================
# WHO may propose, WHO may seal (part 5), WHO holds the constitutional
# rank (tau-nomic's role gate, verdict code 7) - binding a request to a
# person/key is authentication: a fact about the world. Type (A) at the
# root. BUT: everything built ON TOP of the root is in-language again -
# role structure, scoped delegation, separation of powers are just more
# decidable rules (the same meets and entailments you have watched for
# seven parts). The edge is exactly as thick as "is this signature
# genuine" - and no thicker.

# ============================================================================
# EDGE 4: THE RESIDUE OF CHOICE - and of framing
# ============================================================================
# Part 2 was honest: when two proposals are each consistent with the core
# but conflict with EACH OTHER, no algebra picks a winner. tau-nomic
# hands exactly that residue - and nothing more - to a vote (its L2
# mechanism). And beneath every vote lies the deeper human power: WHAT
# gets proposed, WHICH questions are asked, WHOSE encoding is used
# (edge 1). Type (B), permanently. A formalism that claimed to close
# THIS edge would not be safe - it would be a ruler.
#
# ============================================================================
# THE SHAPE OF THE WHOLE THING (series conclusion)
# ============================================================================
#
# What only Tau can:    decide questions about specs AS VALUES - including
#                       over its own state, over all amendments, over all
#                       paths through time (parts 1, 3, 5).
# What tau-nomic makes of it:  a constitution that is un-argue-away-able
#                       where it must be (core, ratchet, eternity clause)
#                       and honestly human where it should be (choice,
#                       framing, translation).
# How:                  one algebra, three uses - living run for the
#                       irreplaceable core, direct queries for law at
#                       scale, human procedure at the named edges.
# Why:                  because history shows constitutions fall by legal
#                       steps and persuadable judges - and because for the
#                       first time, "this core survives every future" is
#                       not a promise. It is arithmetic.
#
# APPENDIX: nomic_09_the_full_palette.tau shows the same machinery with
# richer rights - scoped conditions, exceptions, numeric thresholds,
# temporal preconditions, and a proved guarantee over every possible
# future amendment. The skeleton of parts 1-8 was the curriculum,
# not the ceiling.
#
# APPENDIX II: nomic_10_the_trilemma.tau answers the question this part
# left standing at the outermost edge - who amends the amendment rule? -
# with Tau's u stream (a specification that rewrites itself), a two-step
# coup, self-binding via `this`, and a proved trilemma showing why the
# fixed-spec + law-as-state architecture of parts 3-6 is forced, not
# chosen.
#
# ============================================================================
# END OF THE SERIES
# ============================================================================
